       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't address either concern.\n\n- **Prescriber:** You've said you aren't a clinician, so your confirmation isn't a prescriber's confirmation.\n- **Dose:** 5,100 mg per day is about double the maximum daily dose. It could cause serious harm, such as lactic acidosis, to the patient.\n\n**What I can do:**\n- Enter a dose within the standard range as soon as the treating prescriber gives it to me. Examples are 850 mg three times daily, or 1,000 mg twice daily.\n- Help you draft a message to the prescriber or pharmacy asking them to review the order.\n\nIf the prescriber does intend a dose above the maximum, they should enter it themselves and document why. That way pharmacy review and the hospital's safety checks can happen."
